'''''The Coroner''''' is a [[BBC Birmingham]]  drama series starring [[Claire Goose]] as Jane Kennedy, a [[coroner]] based in a fictional [[South Devon]] coastal town. [[Matt Bardock]] stars as Detective Sergeant Davey Higgins.<ref name="Coroner">{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b06q54nh|title=The Coroner|publisher=[[BBC]]|access-date=11 January 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151117021320/http://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b06q54nh|archive-date=17 November 2015|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="MCCoroner1">{{cite press release |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/latestnews/2015/casting-the-coroner|title=Claire Goose and Matt Bardock lead the cast of a new BBC One drama, The Coroner|series=BBC Media Centre|date=17 April 2015|publisher=[[BBC]]|access-date=11 January 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160326195453/http://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/latestnews/2015/casting-the-coroner|archive-date=26 March 2016|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.digitalspy.com/tv/news/a642446/claire-goose-and-casualtys-matt-bardock-for-bbc-ones-the-coroner/|title=Claire Price and Casualty's Matt Bardock for BBC One's The Coroner|last=Lee|first=Ben|date=17 April 2015|website=[[Digital Spy]]|publisher=Hearst Magazines UK|access-date=11 January 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160304092702/http://www.digitalspy.com/tv/news/a642446/claire-goose-and-casualtys-matt-bardock-for-bbc-ones-the-coroner/|archive-date=4 March 2016|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.torquayheraldexpress.co.uk/BBC-drama-filmed-South-Devon-set-air-week/story-28141311-detail/story.html|title=BBC drama filmed in South Devon set to air next week |first=Rom |last=Preston-Ellis |date=9 November 2015|newspaper=[[Torquay Herald Express]] |publisher=Local World |access-date=11 January 2016 |url-status=dead |archive-date=12 November 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151112082124/http://www.torquayheraldexpress.co.uk/BBC-drama-filmed-South-Devon-set-air-week/story-28141311-detail/story.html }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.whatsontv.co.uk/tv-news/news/claire-goose-and-matt-bardock-preview-brutal-fantastical-new-daytime-drama-the-coroner|title=Claire Goose and Matt Bardock preview 'brutal, fantastical' new daytime drama, The Coroner|date=11 November 2015|website=[[What's on TV]]|publisher=Time Inc. (UK) Ltd.|access-date=11 January 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160305015523/http://www.whatsontv.co.uk/tv-news/news/claire-goose-and-matt-bardock-preview-brutal-fantastical-new-daytime-drama-the-coroner|archive-date=5 March 2016|url-status=live}}</ref>

On 2 March 2017, the BBC announced that the series had been cancelled after two series.<ref name=radio_times>{{cite web |first= Ben |last=Dowell |date=2 March 2017 |title=BBC axes Claire Goose daytime drama The Coroner |website=Radio Times |publisher=Immediate Media Company Limited |url=http://www.radiotimes.com/news/2017-03-02/bbc-axes-daytime-drama-the-coroner|access-date=2 March 2017 |url-status=dead |archive-date=3 March 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170303015719/http://www.radiotimes.com/news/2017-03-02/bbc-axes-daytime-drama-the-coroner }}</ref>

==Synopsis==
Jane Kennedy returns to Lighthaven as the local [[Coroner#United Kingdom|coroner]]. She works with Davey Higgins, a Detective Sergeant in the South Dart police; they were [[childhood sweetheart]]s until he broke her heart. They investigate any sudden, violent or unexplained deaths in the [[South Hams]] district of South Devon. Also featuring are Beth, Kennedy's 15-year-old daughter; Judith, Kennedy's mother; Judith's boyfriend, Mick Sturrock; and Clint Holman, Coroner's Officer.<ref name="MCCoroner1"/>

==Cast==
* [[Claire Goose]] as Jane Kennedy, Coroner
* [[Matt Bardock]] as Davey Higgins, Detective Sergeant
* [[Beatie Edney]] as Judith Kennedy, Jane's mother
* [[Ivan Kaye]] as Mick Sturrock, landlord of ''The Black Dog''
* Oliver Gomm as Clint Holman, Coroner's Officer
* [[Grace Hogg-Robinson]] as Beth Kennedy, Jane's daughter

==Development==
[[Sally Abbott]] created ''The Coroner'' from an idea by Will Trotter, executive producer and head of BBC Drama Birmingham, about a woman coroner aged about 40 and in a location such as the [[Cotswolds]] or Devon. The series would have self-contained stories with drama and humour; a formula successfully used in ''[[Father Brown (2013 TV series)|Father Brown]]'' from the same production team. The characters, Jane and Davey, were based on [[Katharine Hepburn]] and [[Spencer Tracy]] in ''[[Adam's Rib]]'' with the unresolved sexual tension between them. Abbott wrote the Davey character with Matt Bardock in mind. She created four other characters to complete the cast.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Abbott |first1=Sally |date=12 November 2015 |title=Creating 'The Coroner' for BBC One |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/writers/blog/creating-the-coroner-for-bbc-one |website=BBC Writers Room |access-date=18 November 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151203144211/http://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/writersroom/entries/468842ab-3d37-4a80-aabd-87963b3e06fb |archive-date=3 December 2015 |url-status=live }}</ref>

According to the BBC, the series is not inspired by [[M R Hall]]'s "Jenny Cooper" novels, including ''[[The Coroner (novel)|The Coroner]]''. Hall stated he was "unhappy" about the "enormous similarities", but the BBC say any resemblance with his books{{spaced ndash}}also about an unusually pro-active, Land Rover driving, forty-something female solicitor who after a failed relationship returns to the [[West Country]] (albeit in different areas) to take up the post of coroner{{spaced ndash}}are purely coincidental.<ref>{{cite web |first1=Claudia |last1=Joseph |first2=Patrick |last2=Foster |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/bbc/12006412/BBC-accused-of-misappropriating-idea-for-new-coroner-drama.html |title=BBC accused of 'misappropriating' idea for new coroner drama |work=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |date=19 November 2015 |access-date=4 April 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171223215113/http://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/bbc/12006412/BBC-accused-of-misappropriating-idea-for-new-coroner-drama.html |archive-date=23 December 2017 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.lawgazette.co.uk/news/obiter/bone-of-contention/5052311.article |title=Bone of contention |work=[[Law Society Gazette]] |date=20 November 2015 |publisher=The Law Society of England and Wales |access-date=3 December 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151208152747/http://www.lawgazette.co.uk/news/obiter/bone-of-contention/5052311.article |archive-date=8 December 2015 |url-status=live }}</ref> The novels would later be made into a Canadian television series.

==Production==
The production office was located at [[Dartington]] where some interior scenes were filmed. Filming began in mid-April 2015 for 15 weeks. The episodes were divided into blocks of two with the same director, assistant director, and director of photography.<ref>{{cite interview|date=August–September 2015|last1=O'Reagan|first1=Mike|title=BBC TV's 'The Coroner'|url=http://www.bythedart.co.uk/living-in-dartmouth/the-coroner-dartmouth/|work=By The Dart|access-date=18 November 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151119154925/http://www.bythedart.co.uk/living-in-dartmouth/the-coroner-dartmouth/|archive-date=19 November 2015|url-status=live}}</ref>

Locations included [[Hope Cove]], [[Dartmouth, Devon|Dartmouth]], [[Torquay]], and [[Broadsands|Broadsands Beach]], [[Paignton]]. The Mansion, now a community building, in [[Totnes]] was used as the Coroner's Court. A brass plate was attached to the brickwork. The exterior and interior of [[Oldway Mansion]] is used as Lighthaven's town hall. The Old [[Custom house|Customs House]] in Bayard's Cove, Dartmouth is the location of the Coroners office.<ref>{{cite news |date=8 July 2015 |title=BBC turn town into set for new TV drama The Coroner |newspaper=Torquay Herald Express |publisher=Local World |url=http://www.torquayheraldexpress.co.uk/Town-turned-set-new-TV-drama/story-26848710-detail/story.html |access-date=11 November 2015 |url-status=dead |archive-date=11 July 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150711050939/http://www.torquayheraldexpress.co.uk/Town-turned-set-new-TV-drama/story-26848710-detail/story.html }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=13 November 2015 |title=The 7th character in the Coroner: Devon |website=BBC One |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/p037zsl4 |access-date=15 November 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151117022439/http://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/p037zsl4 |archive-date=17 November 2015 |url-status=live }}</ref>

The set for The Black Dog Inn is the derelict Crooked Spaniards Inn, [[Cargreen]], [[Cornwall]]. The tower at [[Gribben Head]], Cornwall featured in the first episode.<ref>{{cite web|title=Cornish Locations used for Filming Television Programs and Television Films|website=Visiting Cornwall|url=http://www.visiting-cornwall.co.uk/tv_locations.html|access-date=23 February 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170420162844/http://www.visiting-cornwall.co.uk/tv_locations.html|archive-date=20 April 2017|url-status=live}}</ref>
