'''Frank E. X. Dance''' (born November 9, 1929, [[Brooklyn]]) is an American communication professor. In 1994–1995, he was John Evans Professor at [[University of Denver]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Faculty Awards & Honors Past Recipients|url=http://www.du.edu/facsen/facultyhonors.html|publisher=University of Denver|access-date=30 May 2013|archive-date=June 3, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130603032005/http://www.du.edu/facsen/facultyhonors.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

==Life==
He graduated from [[Fordham University]] and [[Northwestern University]].
He taught Speech Communication at the University of Wisconsin-Milwaukee until moving to Denver In the 1970’s.

==Legacy==
A scholarship is named for him at [[University of Wisconsin]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Frank E. X. Dance Scholarship|url=http://www4.uwm.edu/letsci/communication/scholarships/dance.cfm|publisher=University of Wisconsin|access-date=30 May 2013|archive-date=March 2, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130302125708/http://www4.uwm.edu/letsci/communication/scholarships/dance.cfm|url-status=live}}</ref>

==Works==
